<!-- ══════════════════════════════════════
     SECTION 3 - WHY NANOTINT FOR PHILADELPHIA
     ══════════════════════════════════════ -->
<section class="nt-why">
  <div class="nt-why__container">

    <div class="nt-why__image-wrap">
      <img
        src="/images/nanotint-window-film-philadelphia-why.jpg"
        alt="Comfortable Philadelphia room with skylight protected by optically clear NanoTint coating"
        title="NanoTint coating for Philadelphia skylights and curved glass"
        width="768"
        height="960"
        loading="lazy"
        class="nt-why__image"
      />
      <div class="nt-why__stat-card">
        <div class="nt-why__stat-item">
          <svg width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="#7CB342" stroke-width="2.5" aria-hidden="true"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M9 12.75L11.25 15 15 9.75M21 12a9 9 0 11-18 0 9 9 0 0118 0z"/></svg>
          <span>Traditional film doesn't cover</span>
        </div>
        <div class="nt-why__stat-divider"></div>
        <div class="nt-why__stat-item">
          <svg width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="#7CB342" stroke-width="2.5" aria-hidden="true"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M9 12.75L11.25 15 15 9.75M21 12a9 9 0 11-18 0 9 9 0 0118 0z"/></svg>
          <span>curved glass, skylights, or plastic</span>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="nt-why__content">
      <span class="nt-why__eyebrow">Why DryWired Liquid NanoTint</span>
      <h2 class="nt-why__headline">NanoTint Coats the Glass Philadelphia's Traditional Films Can't Reach</h2>
      <p class="nt-why__intro">
        Philadelphia's housing stock is full of specialty glass — arched windows in Society Hill brownstones, curved bay windows in Chestnut Hill colonials, and original leaded skylights in Germantown Victorians. Traditional adhesive film cannot bond to those curved surfaces, but liquid nanotint coating Philadelphia projects can be applied directly to shapes, angles, plastics, and roof glass that film installers usually have to decline.
      </p>
      <ul class="nt-why__bullets">
        <li>
          <svg width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" aria-hidden="true"><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="10" stroke="#7CB342" stroke-width="2"/><path d="M8 12l3 3 5-5" stroke="#7CB342" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg>
          Curved glass compatibility for bay windows, arches, domes, skylights, mansard roofs, and specialty atriums
        </li>
        <li>
          <svg width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" aria-hidden="true"><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="10" stroke="#7CB342" stroke-width="2"/><path d="M8 12l3 3 5-5" stroke="#7CB342" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg>
          Interior or exterior application, including roof glass and skylights where the usable surface is outside
        </li>
        <li>
          <svg width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" aria-hidden="true"><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="10" stroke="#7CB342" stroke-width="2"/><path d="M8 12l3 3 5-5" stroke="#7CB342" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg>
          Signal-transparent chemistry with no Wi-Fi, GPS, cellular, or access-control interference
        </li>
        <li>
          <svg width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" aria-hidden="true"><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="10" stroke="#7CB342" stroke-width="2"/><path d="M8 12l3 3 5-5" stroke="#7CB342" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg>
          <span>Plastic, acrylic, and polycarbonate compatibility for greenhouse panels, partitions, and specialty glazing</span>
        </li>
        <li>
          <svg width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" aria-hidden="true"><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="10" stroke="#7CB342" stroke-width="2"/><path d="M8 12l3 3 5-5" stroke="#7CB342" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg>
          <span>Optically clear UV protection for <a href="/benefits/uv-protection/" class="nt-body-link">artwork, floors, fabrics, and collections</a> without visible color shift</span>
        </li>
      </ul>
      <div class="nt-why__climate-facts">
        <div class="nt-why__climate-item">
          <span class="nt-why__climate-num">99%+</span>
          <span class="nt-why__climate-label">UV block</span>
        </div>
        <div class="nt-why__climate-item">
          <span class="nt-why__climate-num">5+</span>
          <span class="nt-why__climate-label">Surface types covered</span>
        </div>
        <div class="nt-why__climate-item">
          <span class="nt-why__climate-num">3</span>
          <span class="nt-why__climate-label">Brush, roller, spray options</span>
        </div>
      </div>
      <p style="font-family:var(--font-body,'DM Sans',sans-serif);font-size:15px;color:var(--text-mid,#4a4a4a);line-height:1.7;margin:0 0 18px;">"Brush, roller, or spray," according to the DryWired Liquid NanoTint installation guide, are approved application methods for the coating. For solar comfort, see our <a href="/benefits/energy-savings/" class="nt-body-link">energy savings guidance</a>; for office and institutional specialty glass, see <a href="/applications/office/" class="nt-body-link">office window film applications</a>. UV risk is also explained in the <a href="https://www.epa.gov/sunsafety/uv-index-scale-0" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="nt-body-link">EPA UV Index guidance</a>.</p>
      <a href="/contact/" class="nt-why__cta">
        Get a specialty glass assessment &rarr;
        <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.5" aria-hidden="true"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M4.5 12h15m0 0l-6.75-6.75M19.5 12l-6.75 6.75"/></svg>
      </a>
    </div>

  </div>
</section>

<!-- ══════════════════════════════════════
     SECTION 4 - RESIDENTIAL / COMMERCIAL SLIDER
     ══════════════════════════════════════ -->
<section class="nt-slider" id="ntSlider">
  <div class="nt-slider__track" id="ntTrack">

    <!-- SLIDE 01: Residential -->
    <div class="nt-slider__slide" data-slide="0">
      <img src="/images/nanotint-window-film-philadelphia-residential.jpg" alt="Philadelphia rowhome specialty glass protected with NanoTint coating"
          title="NanoTint residential coating for Philadelphia specialty glass" class="nt-slider__bg" loading="lazy" />
      <div class="nt-slider__overlay"></div>
      <div class="nt-slider__content">
        <div class="nt-slider__step">01</div>
        <h2 class="nt-slider__title">Philadelphia homes with specialty glass</h2>
        <p class="nt-slider__desc">Rowhomes, curved windows, and skylights often have surfaces that film can't reach. NanoTint coats any compatible surface with UV and heat protection while keeping clear glass visually natural.</p>
        <div class="nt-slider__faq">
          <div class="nt-slider__faq-item">
            <button class="nt-slider__faq-q" aria-expanded="false">Can NanoTint protect historic arched glass?<span class="nt-slider__faq-icon" aria-hidden="true">+</span></button>
            <div class="nt-slider__faq-a" hidden>Yes. NanoTint is well suited to arched and specialty glass because the liquid follows the shape of the surface instead of depending on a flat adhesive sheet.</div>
          </div>
          <div class="nt-slider__faq-item">
            <button class="nt-slider__faq-q" aria-expanded="false">Will clear NanoTint change the view?<span class="nt-slider__faq-icon" aria-hidden="true">+</span></button>
            <div class="nt-slider__faq-a" hidden>Liquid NanoTint Clear is optically clear, so it protects against UV exposure and infrared heat without a visible tint or color shift.</div>
          </div>
          <div class="nt-slider__faq-item">
            <button class="nt-slider__faq-q" aria-expanded="false">Can it go on skylights at any angle?<span class="nt-slider__faq-icon" aria-hidden="true">+</span></button>
            <div class="nt-slider__faq-a" hidden>Yes. NanoTint can be specified for angled skylights and roof glass after the surface, access, and exposure are reviewed.</div>
          </div>
        </div>
        <a href="/contact/" class="nt-slider__cta">Get a residential estimate &rarr;</a>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- SLIDE 02: Commercial -->
    <div class="nt-slider__slide" data-slide="1">
      <img src="/images/nanotint-window-film-philadelphia-commercial.jpg" alt="Philadelphia commercial atrium with curved glass protected by NanoTint coating"
          title="NanoTint commercial specialty glass coating Philadelphia" class="nt-slider__bg" loading="lazy" />
      <div class="nt-slider__overlay"></div>
      <div class="nt-slider__content">
        <div class="nt-slider__step">02</div>
        <h2 class="nt-slider__title">Commercial glass beyond film's reach</h2>
        <p class="nt-slider__desc">Museum atriums, hospital skylights, and curved curtain wall create shapes traditional installers turn away. NanoTint handles glass geometry, plastic panels, and access conditions that adhesive film cannot.</p>
