    <div class="nt-pl-row__content">
      <span class="nt-pl-row__num">02</span>
      <span class="nt-pl-row__eyebrow">Skylights · Arches · Atriums · Specialty Shapes</span>
      <h3 class="nt-pl-row__heading">The Only UV Coating That Works on Philadelphia's Curved and Specialty Glass</h3>
      <p class="nt-pl-row__body">Curved surfaces are the one thing traditional film cannot reliably do. A flat adhesive sheet wrinkles, lifts, or bubbles when forced onto compound curves, arched skylights, domes, and shaped architectural glass. NanoTint is different because the coating is applied as a liquid and cures in place.</p>
      <p class="nt-pl-row__body">Philadelphia use cases include museum skylights near the Parkway, historic arched windows in Society Hill and Chestnut Hill, hospital atriums at Penn Medicine and Jefferson, curved restaurant glass, and specialty glazing at universities. NanoTint window film in Philadelphia gives those projects a UV-control path without replacing original or custom glass.</p>

      <div class="nt-pl-row__specs">
        <div class="nt-pl-row__spec"><span class="nt-pl-row__spec-val">Curved</span><span class="nt-pl-row__spec-label">Curved Glass</span></div>
