      <h3 class="nt-pl-row__heading">NanoTint for Polycarbonate, Acrylic, and Non-Glass Surfaces</h3>
      <p class="nt-pl-row__body">Traditional window film is designed for glass and usually struggles on plastic, acrylic, and polycarbonate because adhesives can fail, haze, or react poorly with the substrate. NanoTint specialty variants give Philadelphia projects another option for surfaces that still need UV control and heat reduction.</p>
      <p class="nt-pl-row__body">Common projects include greenhouse panels, polycarbonate skylights, acrylic partitions, specialty commercial panels, and marine glass around Penn's Landing. Film doesn't bond to many of these surfaces with the reliability owners need; NanoTint does when the surface is compatible and properly prepared.</p>

      <div class="nt-pl-row__specs">
        <div class="nt-pl-row__spec"><span class="nt-pl-row__spec-val">Poly</span><span class="nt-pl-row__spec-label">Polycarbonate</span></div>
