      <p class="nt-casestudy__lead">The owner of a historic Chestnut Hill Victorian had original curved bay windows and a small skylight that were allowing UV exposure into rooms with antique floors, fabrics, and furniture.</p>
      <p class="nt-casestudy__body">Three window film companies had already turned down the job because adhesive film could not bond correctly to the curved glass. Window replacement would have changed the historic character of the home and introduced a much larger construction project.</p>
      <p class="nt-casestudy__body">NanoTint was applied by brush to the curved surfaces, including the skylight. The cured coating delivered 99% UV protection without a visible change to the glass, preserving the home's original look while solving the exposure problem.</p>
